  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The vector $a$ has magnitude $2$, the vector $b$ has magnitude $9$, the angle between $a$ and $b$ is ${45}^{\u2218}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $a\\times b.$ Find $a\\times b$ in terms of $n.$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|a|\\cdot |b|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =2\\cdot 9\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{45}^{\u2218}\\cdot n \\\\  & =18\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot n \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{2}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
